<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <!--
    Content Security Policy notes
    - script-src allows exactly two inline scripts by SHA-256 hash:
        'sha256-MdMapQxvxeL6vP8KdU8o5Ie9nNnnk3l94+maA3yW+k8='  the MathJax config block below
        'sha256-ieoeWczDHkReVBsRBqaal5AFMlBtNjMzgwKvLqi/tSU='  Cloudflare Web Analytics' edge-injected beacon
      If you edit the MathJax block, CI (scripts/ci/check-csp.py) recomputes the hash and
      fails with the new value to paste here. If Cloudflare changes its beacon, analytics
      stops and DevTools shows the new hash in a CSP error.
    - base-uri / form-action / object-src are locked because Markdown content may contain
      raw HTML (html: true), so the template must not trust the body.
    - frame-ancestors cannot be set in a <meta> CSP; X-Frame-Options: DENY in _headers covers it.
  -->
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
        content="default-src 'self';
                 script-src 'self' 'sha256-MdMapQxvxeL6vP8KdU8o5Ie9nNnnk3l94+maA3yW+k8=' 'sha256-ieoeWczDHkReVBsRBqaal5AFMlBtNjMzgwKvLqi/tSU=' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3.2.2/ https://static.cloudflareinsights.com;
                 style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
                 img-src 'self' data: https:;
                 font-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3.2.2/;
                 connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com;
                 frame-src https://player.vimeo.com https://www.youtube.com;
                 base-uri 'self';
                 form-action 'none';
                 object-src 'none';" />
  {%- set pageDescription = description or "Jesse Wolfson, a professor in the Department of Mathematics at the University of California, Irvine. Research on the interplay of arithmetic, geometry, and topology." -%}
  <title>{% if title %}{{ title }} – {% endif %}Jesse Wolfson</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ pageDescription }}" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="{% if title %}{{ title }} – {% endif %}Jesse Wolfson" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ pageDescription }}" />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://jpwolfson.com{{ page.url }}" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css" />
  <!-- CSP hash for this script: sha256-MdMapQxvxeL6vP8KdU8o5Ie9nNnnk3l94+maA3yW+k8= (referenced in script-src above) -->
  <script>
    MathJax = {
      tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$'], ['\\(', '\\)']] },
      options: { skipHtmlTags: ['script','noscript','style','textarea','pre'] }
    };
  </script>
  <!--
    MathJax – pinned to an exact version with Subresource Integrity.
    CI (scripts/ci/check-sri.sh) re-downloads this file and fails if the hash drifts.
    To update: change the version, then run the command printed by that script.
  -->
  <script async src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3.2.2/es5/tex-chtml.js"
          integrity="sha384-AHAnt9ZhGeHIrydA1Kp1L7FN+2UosbF7RQg6C+9Is/a7kDpQ1684C2iH2VWil6r4"
          crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>
  <header>
    <div class="site-title"><a href="/">Jesse Wolfson</a></div>
    <nav>
      {%- set navItems = [
        ["/working-group/", "Working Group"],
        ["/papers/", "Papers"],
        ["/talks/", "Talks"],
        ["/mathematics-and-dance/", "Mathematics and Dance"],
        ["/teaching/", "Teaching"],
        ["/workshops/", "Workshops"],
        ["/roosevelt-institute/", "Roosevelt Institute"],
        ["/cv/", "CV"]
      ] %}
      {%- for item in navItems %}
      <a href="{{ item[0] }}"{% if page.url == item[0] %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item[1] }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    {{ content | safe }}
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>Jesse Wolfson &middot; University of California, Irvine</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
